# Copy to .env. Offline (MockPlanner / MockLLM) needs none of this.
#
# The real-model path is model-agnostic at the protocol boundary: any local
# runtime that serves OpenAI-compatible /v1/chat/completions can be used
# (vLLM, llama.cpp server, Ollama proxy, or a site-specific adapter).
#
# The planning assumption is a capable local model, roughly "good 120B-class".
# The model is still untrusted and only proposes QuerySpec JSON.

# --- Local model — production posture (no data egress) ---
# SAFETRE_LLM=real
# SAFETRE_LLM_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1
# SAFETRE_LLM_API_KEY=local
# SAFETRE_LLM_MODEL=local-120b
# SAFETRE_LLM_TEMPERATURE=0
# SAFETRE_LLM_TIMEOUT=60
# SAFETRE_ALLOWED_LLM_HOSTS=localhost,127.0.0.1,::1

# --- Synthetic-data dev only: remote endpoint opt-in ---
# SAFETRE_LLM=real
# SAFETRE_ALLOW_REMOTE_LLM=1
# SAFETRE_LLM_BASE_URL=https://example-llm-provider.invalid/v1
# SAFETRE_LLM_API_KEY=dev-key
# SAFETRE_LLM_MODEL=provider/model-name

# --- Disclosure policy overrides (optional) ---
# These override config.yaml; config.yaml overrides the built-in defaults.
# SAFETRE_MIN_CELL=10
# SAFETRE_MAX_OUTPUT_ROWS=100
# SAFETRE_QUERY_BUDGET=20
# SAFETRE_DIFFERENCING_DELTA=10
# SAFETRE_DOM_THRESHOLD=0.5
# SAFETRE_INFLUENCE_THRESHOLD=0.5
# SAFETRE_ROUND_BASE=5
# Dominance for SECOND-MOMENT cells (sums of squares), which back a model's
# standard errors. Unset means the same bound as any other magnitude — but the
# same number is a far tighter rule on a squared scale, so state it if you
# want models to be available (docs/acro-integration.md §3).
# SAFETRE_MOMENT2_DOM_THRESHOLD=0.8
# SAFETRE_CONFIG=config.yaml           # path to the policy file
#
# Response-time control (spec R18). Every response is held to the next
# multiple of the quantum and work past the ceiling is refused, so latency
# cannot rank the cohorts suppression hides. Set the quantum equal to the
# ceiling for constant time; set it to 0 to disable and reopen the channel.
# SAFETRE_RESPONSE_QUANTUM_MS=50
# SAFETRE_RESPONSE_CEILING_MS=5000
#
# Which rules vet a cell: "standin" or "standin+external", the two composed so
# a cell is suppressed if either says so. An external checker is never the only
# vetter — it has no egress rules and no complementary suppression.
# Leave SAFETRE_VETTER unset and a checker is used whenever SAFETRE_CHECKER_CMD
# is set; name it explicitly to REQUIRE one, and startup then fails if the
# command is missing rather than running without it. Either way the release
# records which rules decided it.
# SAFETRE_VETTER=standin+external
# SAFETRE_CHECKER_CMD=uv run --no-default-groups --group acro python redteam/acro_checker.py

# --- Safepod / restricted-channel controls ---
# In production the app should only accept traffic from the restricted channel
# gateway. For the tailscale-serve topology, the gateway talks to uvicorn over
# localhost, so loopback is the only allowed peer.
# SAFETRE_RESTRICTED_CHANNEL=1
# SAFETRE_CHANNEL_ALLOW_NETS=127.0.0.1/32,::1/128
# SAFETRE_REQUIRE_IDENTITY=1
# SAFETRE_ALLOWLIST=alex@example.org,sam@example.org
#
# The Tailscale-User-Login header is trusted only over a loopback-only channel.
# If you widen SAFETRE_CHANNEL_ALLOW_NETS, you MUST assert a trusted upstream
# proxy that sets/strips the header, or identity fails closed:
# SAFETRE_TRUST_FORWARDED_IDENTITY=1
# Optional extra gate: require the proxy to present a shared secret header
# (X-Safetre-Proxy-Auth) before the identity header is believed.
# SAFETRE_PROXY_SHARED_SECRET=load-from-off-box-secret

# --- Audit log ---
# SAFETRE_AUDIT_DB=/var/lib/safetre/audit.db
# SAFETRE_AUDIT_KEY=load-from-off-box-secret
# Off-box anchor of the chain head; /api/audit/verify checks against it when set.
# SAFETRE_AUDIT_HEAD_ANCHOR=<hex head captured off-box>
